    "original_text": "Attributed scoped mathematical restatement with explicit remaining producer:\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space, including dimension zero, with its Borel measurable space. f:E->R is globally C2. kappa>=1 and every genuine nested second derivative satisfies (2kappa)^-1||v||^2 <= D2f(z)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for every z,v. These are the normalized smoothed-potential curvature interface; f=V_eta and Lemma4.1 are independent prerequisites.\nJ>=2,h>0. The nodes are t_j=h/2(1-cos(j*pi/(J-1))), ell_j their actual Lagrange cardinal polynomials, Lambda=sup_{s in[0,h]} sum_j|ell_j(s)|, omega_ij=integral_0^{t_i}(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds, b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds and c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds. Assume only h^2 Lambda<=1. In particular h<=1 is derived, never added as a premise.\na=exp(-h/2),sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)),Gamma=stdGaussian(E) product stdGaussian(E). Both Gaussian vectors are independent under Gamma and shared synchronously between compared inputs. P0=a p+sigma zeta0; Y0_j=x+t_j P0; Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij gradient f(Y0_j); Phi=(x+hP0-sum_j c_j gradient f(Y1_j),a(P0-sum_j b_j gradient f(Y1_j))+sigma zeta1). No stochastic gradient/proximal array appears.\nFor every pair z,zprime and every Gaussian vector zeta (not just almost surely), H_j is the ordinary Bochner integral of the Riesz-represented genuine D2f along the Y1prime_j-to-Y1_j segment; H=h^-1 sum_j b_j H_j. The source phase norm is the Euclidean L2 product WithLp2, not the default product max norm.\nAt this explicit normalized C2 curvature interface, the actual exact-gradient two-Picard map Phi is measurable and defines a Markov kernel K(z)=Gamma.map(Phi_z). For every synchronously coupled input pair and every two-vector noise value, the actual integral average H is symmetric, (2kappa)^-1 I<=H<=I and ||H||op<=1. There exists a genuine continuous real linear R on the L2 phase space such that Delta1=Delta0+h*(Delta p,-H Delta x-Delta p)+R Delta0 and ||R||op<=8 Lambda h^2. R may depend on z,zprime,zeta; no measurable choice or global derivative of Phi is asserted. H, Phi, K and the remainder are constructed, not supplied as conclusion certificates.\nThis is the actual deterministic numerical kernel/first-order difference interface in Lemma4.6, conditional on the explicitly exposed normalized C2 curvature producer. The identity f=V_eta and source Lemma4.1 smoothing/curvature production remain open. It does not prove Proposition4.7 contraction/step absorption, Lemma4.8 M_kappa increment, logarithmic Lambda/B2, Khat/Kbar accuracy, invariance, repeated-history/cost, PBPS, either complete main theorem or their actual-input expected-cost composition. Khat and Kbar cannot be replaced by this K; TV closeness cannot transfer unbounded cost.",
    "text_sha256": "80fe9844c40e3dcaffe9528d557399ed0a025486c4d7eaec49fa69a51829be6b"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.FirstOrderDifference.source_first_order_difference",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/FirstOrderDifference.lean",
    "statement": "{f : E → ℝ} {κ h : ℝ} {J : ℕ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)\n    (hH : ∀ z v, (1 / (2 * κ)) * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ f) z v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ f) z v) v ≤ ‖v‖ ^ 2)\n    (hJ : 2 ≤ J) (hh : 0 < h) :\n    let t := fun i : Fin J => h/2*(1-Real.cos ((i : ℝ)/(J-1 : ℝ)*Real.pi))\n    let ell := fun j : Fin J => Lagrange.basis Finset.univ t j\n    let Λ := sSup ((fun s : ℝ => ∑ j : Fin J, |(ell j).eval s|) '' Icc 0 h)\n    let ω := fun i j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..t i, (t i-s)*(ell j).eval s\n    let b := fun j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..h, (ell j).eval s\n    let c := fun j : Fin J => ∫ s in 0..h, (h-s)*(ell j).eval s\n    h ^ 2 * Λ ≤ 1 →\n    let a := Real.exp (-h / 2)\n    let sigma := Real.sqrt (1 - Real.exp (-h))\n    let Γ := (stdGaussian E).prod (stdGaussian E)\n    let P0 := fun (z ζ : E × E) => a • z.2 + sigma • ζ.1\n    let Y0 := fun (z ζ : E × E) j => z.1 + t j • P0 z ζ\n    let Y1 := fun (z ζ : E × E) i => Y0 z ζ i - ∑ j, ω i j • gradient f (Y0 z ζ j)\n    let Φ := fun w : (E × E) × (E × E) =>\n      (w.1.1 + h • P0 w.1 w.2 - ∑ j, c j • gradient f (Y1 w.1 w.2 j),\n        a • (P0 w.1 w.2 - ∑ j, b j • gradient f (Y1 w.1 w.2 j)) + sigma • w.2.2)\n    Measurable Φ ∧\n      (∃ K : Kernel (E × E) (E × E), IsMarkovKernel K ∧\n        ∀ z, K z = Γ.map (fun ζ => Φ (z, ζ))) ∧\n      ∀ z z' ζ : E × E,\n        let H := h⁻¹ • ∑ j, b j •\n          (∫ u in (0 : ℝ)..1, InnerProductSpace.continuousLinearMapOfBilin\n            (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ f)\n              (Y1 z' ζ j + u • (Y1 z ζ j - Y1 z' ζ j))))\n        let d := WithLp.toLp 2 (z.1 - z'.1, z.2 - z'.2)\n        H.toLinearMap.IsSymmetric ∧\n          (∀ v, (1 / (2 * κ)) * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ (H v) v ∧\n            inner ℝ (H v) v ≤ ‖v‖ ^ 2) ∧ ‖H‖ ≤ 1 ∧\n          ∃ R : WithLp 2 (E × E) →L[ℝ] WithLp 2 (E × E),\n            ‖R‖ ≤ 8 * Λ * h ^ 2 ∧\n            WithLp.toLp 2 ((Φ (z,ζ)).1 - (Φ (z',ζ)).1,\n              (Φ (z,ζ)).2 - (Φ (z',ζ)).2) =\n                d + h • WithLp.toLp 2 (z.2-z'.2, -H (z.1-z'.1)-(z.2-z'.2)) + R d",
    "statement_sha256": "8cf24bcdd5f6794e0055b983ccca5b97d0ab1b7d525426c82e90ff76e1d22b8e",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space, endowed with its Borel measurable space. f is a real-valued map. ContDiff R 2 f means global twice continuously Frechet differentiable; fderiv R (fderiv R f) is the genuine nested second derivative. gradient f is its first derivative Riesz representative, not an independently supplied map.",
      "Lagrange.basis gives the actual cardinal polynomial at the defined nodes; polynomial.eval is evaluation. sSup of the displayed real set is its real supremum. Integral s in a..b is ordinary Lebesgue Bochner interval integration. Fin J indexes0 through J-1.",
      "stdGaussian E is the standard isotropic Gaussian law associated to the real Euclidean inner product. Measure.prod means independent product, Measure.map means pushforward. Kernel(E x E)(E x E) is a measurable family of measures on phase space; IsMarkovKernel means each is a probability measure. Measurable Phi is joint measurability in phase input and both noise coordinates.",
      "continuousLinearMapOfBilin is the Riesz-represented operator of the genuine continuous bilinear form: inner(A v,w)=B(v,w). H.IsSymmetric means all-vector inner(Hv,w)=inner(v,Hw). ||H|| is the induced operator norm, not a supplied certificate.",
      "WithLp2(E x E) is the Euclidean product vector space with norm sqrt(||x||^2+||p||^2), coordinatewise addition/scalar action. toLp2 embeds the pair into that normed copy; it does not change coordinates. R is a continuous real linear operator on that L2 phase space. R is existential inside all compared-input/noise quantifiers."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Complete actual phase/Markov/difference production and genuine nonconstant positive-Hessian potential Test passed; standard3 only. Independent source review pending."
